    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "",
      "id": 8,
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 21,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 3
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "### Business dimensions\nBoomi cannot attach custom HTTP headers to a span, so `consumerId`, `responseCode` and the rest are parsed out of **Notify shape messages** by the collector. They therefore sit on the Notify span, not the API root span \u2014 which is why these panels show **counts and outcomes per consumer, but not latency per consumer**. Latency lives on the root span above. To get per-consumer latency, add an exit Notify that logs `consumerId` alongside elapsed ms (`1-APIEntryLogger` already records `txnapiStartTime`)."
      }
    },
